"""Inorganic objectives for the articulations of the ACS inorganic content map (2018) that no Library objective
answered: Slater's rules, symmetry-derived polarity and chirality, the isolobal analogy, ligand sterics, Werner
isomers and nomenclature, Born–Haber cycles, defects, semiconductors and superconductors, framework materials,
substitution and electron-transfer mechanisms, the trans and chelate effects, fluxionality, formation constants,
nonaqueous acid–base chemistry, chiral catalysis, LFSE and hydration, d–d spectra, magnetic measurement,
multinuclear NMR, sensors and safe technique. Numeric keys are recomputed along another route (electron counts from
pt_group, LFSE from incalc's cfse, Hess cycles solved, linear charge balances solved); facts are authored."""
